  {:id :s6a-plan-02
   :resolution "P1 is wholly offline. Table-driven inert payload/outcome pairs prove preparation, refusal and outcome classification only. Each impossible pair has a reasoned not-applicable classification; it is not a skipped actual transport assertion. No injected case proves an actual send, revocation, DNS, redirect, proxy or downstream isolation. Working fake HTTP and isolated downstream controls remain P2; authentic signed-policy and transformation proofs remain P3/P4."}
  {:id :s6a-plan-03
   :resolution "Accept only explicitly enumerated bounded plain representations at a demonstrably safe host boundary; refuse metadata, records, JS objects, accessors, proxies and poisoned persistent backing storage before traversal/coercion. Instrument actual zero-accessor controls. If a representation cannot be inspected safely, deny it; do not claim universal reflection/proxy safety. Known structured image/data-URI/attachment/binary variants deny, but no arbitrary-string test can detect every encoding. P1's synthetic text is inert prepared data with authority none, not authenticated content provenance. Real source/byte/read-scope authority remains held."}
  {:id :s6a-plan-04
   :resolution "Restrict P1 to EXACTLY ONE explicitly synthetic user text message with a closed source-event, content-reference, revision and optional named derivation binding. Empty or multiple messages, non-user role, caller completeness flags, implicit history recovery/trimming/summarization and opaque serialized tool/image envelopes deny. Multi-message preparation requires a separately reviewed ordered-history/completeness contract before expansion. This narrower source test phase does not silently narrow whole-task acceptance."}]
